claimed: flush-op — Flush as a real operation in the row (the half of the user's request chunk-flush did not deliver): a producer that knows where a message ends (an LLM turn, a frame) says so, and the chunking feed emits what it holds without waiting for the chunk to fill or for flushAfter to expire. Shape: a one-constructor signature with its own TypeableK, interpreted by the feed's own walk of the program (relay cannot serve -- its handler answers with a value, while Flush must emit an Async send at that point). Plain sources widen into the flushing row so there is ONE accumulation path, not two; measure that the widen pass costs the chunked path nothing.
